WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.571
Select an operating-system image that supports the accelerator and the intended framework.

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:14.442
A provider image with validated drivers and CUDA can shorten setup, but its versions still need to match the application.

00:00:14.442 --> 00:00:20.425
Verify the GPU at the operating-system level, then run a small framework operation.

00:00:20.425 --> 00:00:26.821
Detection alone does not prove that model inference or training will use acceleration correctly.

00:00:26.821 --> 00:00:36.931
Containers can package the application, libraries, and model server into a repeatable unit while relying on a compatible host driver and GPU runtime.

00:00:36.931 --> 00:00:40.851
Pin container images to known versions or digests.

00:00:40.851 --> 00:00:46.421
If using Python environments directly, isolate dependencies and record exact package versions.

00:00:46.421 --> 00:00:51.992
Notebooks are effective for exploration but should not become undocumented production servers.

00:00:51.992 --> 00:00:55.087
Secure SSH before beginning model work.

00:00:55.087 --> 00:01:02.308
Restrict source addresses, use managed or short-lived keys where possible, and remove default or stale credentials.

00:01:02.308 --> 00:01:06.228
Bind notebooks and model servers to private interfaces.

00:01:06.228 --> 00:01:13.036
Reach them through an authenticated gateway or secure tunnel rather than opening administrative ports broadly.

00:01:13.036 --> 00:01:19.020
Keep API keys and model-repository tokens out of scripts, notebooks, and machine images.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:28.304
Begin with a simple manual path: start the instance, verify acceleration, load one model, run one representative request, and shut down.

00:01:28.304 --> 00:01:32.636
Record commands, versions, ports, storage mounts, and expected output.

00:01:32.636 --> 00:01:41.096
Once the path is proven, automate it with reviewed setup scripts or images and test on a fresh rental.

00:01:41.096 --> 00:01:47.491
Reproducible setup saves billable troubleshooting time and makes an instance replaceable instead of precious.
